First, perform the requested integration.

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\displaystyle\int\limits_{0}^{1}{f\left( x \right)dx}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\int_0^1\sum_{n=0}^{\infty }\dfrac{n+2}{2^{n}}x^{n+1}dx
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\sum_{n=0}^{\infty }\int_0^1\dfrac{n+2}{2^{n}}x^{n+1}dx
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\left. \sum_{n=0}^{\infty }\dfrac{n+2}{2^{n}}\dfrac{x^{n+2}}{n+2} \right|_{0}^{1}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\sum_{n=0}^{\infty }{\dfrac{1}{{{2}^n}}}
\end{align}$
